35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The supplier quotes show delivery windows slip when larger clients book first.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The bus links are gone in the outer wards, so we must go to them.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The grant pays session fees for twelve months, then the flat budget takes over.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The old digitisation project failed because no one owned the indexing, but the evening groups survived.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that volunteers run the repair clinic, but no staff member is trained to supervise them.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, If the roads close, how do we get the equipment to the halls?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, We can’t. That is why the outreach model worked; we brought the service to them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, The vehicle line overran by a third last year. We cannot afford the fuel.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, That is the gap. The evening groups worked because the volunteers were self-managing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, Yes, but if we add a new service, who checks that the volunteers are actually qualified?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, If the vehicle line is over, we cannot rely on central dispatch for remote areas.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, Exactly. The data shows the outer wards are the only ones with real demand.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, But the endowment covers capital, not the recurring costs of running those vehicles.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, The old programmes show that low-cost, volunteer-led models are the only ones that stick.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I agree. A model that relies on existing volunteers without new staff training is safer.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I am leaning toward a model that does not depend on our vehicles or suppliers.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I am pushing for the outreach option. It is the only one that reaches the people who lost the bus.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I am concerned about the recurring costs. The grant ends, and the flat budget is already thin.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I am voting for the option that uses the existing volunteer infrastructure. It has a track record.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am worried about the supervision gap. We need a candidate that does not require new certifications.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
